# Root .env — read by docker compose only.
#
# Application configuration lives in backend/.env and frontend/.env; this file
# holds just the values compose itself interpolates.
#   cp .env.example .env

# --- container ports (host side) -------------------------------------------
# Defaults avoid 5432/6379 so a locally installed Postgres or Redis keeps working.
POSTGRES_PORT=5433
REDIS_PORT=6381

# --- database bootstrap ----------------------------------------------------
POSTGRES_USER=marketcompass
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=marketcompass
POSTGRES_DB=marketcompass

# --- adapters used by the containerised backend ----------------------------
MC_BROKER_PROVIDER=mock

# AI Console / copilot LLM provider. Leave as rule_based to run with no API key
# (deterministic canned guidance). Switch to anthropic to power the AI Console
# with Claude. The provider factory degrades back to rule_based if the key is
# blank or the SDK isn't installed, so the app always boots.
#
# To enable Claude:
#   1. install the SDK:   cd backend && uv sync --extra llm
#   2. set the three vars below (get a key at https://console.anthropic.com/)
MC_LLM_PROVIDER=rule_based
MC_LLM_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Claude model the AI Console calls. Defaults to claude-sonnet-5 (the code
# default) when left blank. Options:
#   claude-opus-5     - most capable, highest cost
#   claude-sonnet-5   - balanced (default)
#   claude-haiku-4-5  - fastest / cheapest
MC_LLM_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# --- Claude setup, for reference -------------------------------------------
# MC_LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
# MC_LLM_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# MC_LLM_MODEL=claude-opus-5

# OpenRouter (https://openrouter.ai) — one key, many models via an OpenAI-
# compatible endpoint. Uses its own namespaced model id, not MC_LLM_MODEL.
MC_LLM_OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
MC_LLM_OPENROUTER_MODEL=anthropic/claude-3.7-sonnet
# --- OpenRouter setup, for reference ---------------------------------------
# MC_LLM_PROVIDER=openrouter
# MC_LLM_OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-...
# MC_LLM_OPENROUTER_MODEL=openai/gpt-4o